81. What is a transaction?
"A transaction is a collection of SQL operations treated as a single unit. Either all changes are saved or none are saved."
START TRANSACTION;

UPDATE accounts
SET balance = balance - 1000
WHERE acc_id = 1;

UPDATE accounts
SET balance = balance + 1000
WHERE acc_id = 2;
COMMIT;

Output
Before:
acc_id	balance
1	      5000
2	      3000

After COMMIT:
acc_id	balance
 1      4000
 2     	4000














































































































